    },
    "body": "Fix for #2043. Main uses squash merges, so a merged branch's HEAD is never an ancestor of `origin/main`, and the first `--apply` skipped exactly the worktrees it was written to remove. A worktree now counts as merged on ancestry **or** an exact match with a merged PR's `headRefOid` (via `gh`). It is still kept when dirty or busy.\n\nTest: a scratch worktree on the merged `claude/storage-hygiene` branch (head = #2043's merged head) is now listed as \"would remove\"; a dirty worktree is still kept. `bash -n` clean.\n\nReferences #2037\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
